  "reply": "Almost certainly not. Today is October 29, so the month ends in two days, and most of the epic is still open.\n\nThis thread's workstream has no items yet, so I searched outside it. The checkout epic is SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards. What follows is read-only, from the change history Oriel keeps.\n\n- **Where it stands:** 5 of its 14 items are done. 4 are in progress and 5 haven't started. The first chart below breaks this down.\n- **Pace:** Items have been finishing at about 0.8 a week since early September. At that rate, Oriel's forecast puts the last 9 around **January 14**, and probably somewhere between December 21 and March 16. That assumes no new items are added. The second chart shows this.\n- **What's stuck:** The 5 items not started have all been waiting 53–57 days. They include SYN-88 Refund to the original payment method when a sailing is cancelled and SYN-57 Checkout analytics: drop-off by step, which are the two biggest by estimate. SYN-21 Update the payment declined error message has also been in progress for 22 days. The two tables below list who owns each open item.\n\nOriel's separate Checkout workstream may be a better home for this question. If you want, I can add the epic's items to this workstream so you can follow it here."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast. A yes or no to the question that follows from Oriel's forecast is not one of its own.
